From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <darknagel@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:07:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 94/95] linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250: video codec voltage,
 Venus clock, encoder size

Kernel 0223-0224: the video codec votes MMCX, and its OPP table gives the
core clock rates, so the video core no longer runs at 1332 MHz on a
LOW_SVS vote when the display is off. Decoding with the display off
corrupted frames before.
Kernel 0225: Venus scales vcodec0_core on SM8250.
Kernel 0226: the Iris encoder encodes the requested size instead of
scaling the aligned buffer into it.
